<div id="block-moc-content" class="block block-system block-system-main-block">  <div class="layout layout--onecol">
    <div class="layout__region layout__region--content"><div class="block-region-content"><div class="views-element-container block block-views block-views-blockmajor-statistics-block-1">    <h1>Production and Supplies</h1><div><div class="view view-major-statistics view-id-major_statistics view-display-id-block_1 js-view-dom-id-cc2e165603a528f2e9bbb1f627b4ab42cd0675760494635d276e005fe7bae45a">    <div class="view-content">  <div class="views-row"><img src="/sites/default/files/2019-08/pr17.jpg" width="288" height="192" alt="Production And Supplies" typeof="foaf:Image" >
<p><a aira-label="Download PDF file on REFORMS ACHIEVEMENTS OF MINISTRY OF COAL SINCE 2014 open in new tab" href="/sites/default/files/2022-06/14-06-2022a-wn.pdf" style="text-decoration:none;color:#000;" target="_blanck">REFORMS &amp; ACHIEVEMENTS OF MINISTRY OF COAL SINCE 2014</a></p>

<h2>COAL PRODUCTION</h2>

<p style="text-align: justify; ">Through sustained programme of investment and greater thrust on application of modern technologies, it has been possible to raise the All India production of coal at <strong>997</strong><b>.83</b> million tonnes in <b>2023-24</b>. The all India Production of coal during <b>2024-25 </b>was <strong>1047.523</strong><b> MT</b>  with a positive growth of <strong>4.98%</strong><b>.</b></p>

<p style="text-align: justify; ">Coal India Limited (CIL) and its subsidiaries accounted for <b>773.81</b> <strong>MT</strong> during <b>2023-24</b> as compared to a production of <strong>703</strong><b>.20</b> <strong>MT</strong> in <b>2022-23</b> showing a positive growth of <strong>10.04%</strong><b>.</b> Coal production of CIL during <b>2024-25</b> was <strong>781.056 MT</strong> with a positive growth of <strong>0.94</strong><b>%.</b></p>

<p style="text-align: justify; ">Singareni Collieries Company Limited (SCCL) is the main source for supply of coal to the southern region. The company produced <strong>70.02</strong> million tonnes of coal during <strong>2023-24</strong> as against <strong>67.14 MT</strong> during the same period of previous year. SCCL production of coal during <strong>2024-25</strong> was <strong>69.01 MT</strong> with a positive growth of <strong>2.8%</strong>. Small quantities of coal are also produced by TISCO, IISCO, DVC and others.</p>

<p>2025-2026</p>

