<h2>COAL DISTRIBUTION AND MARKETING</h2>

<p>The Marketing Division of CIL coordinates marketing activities for all its subsidiaries. CIL has set up Regional Sales Offices and Sub-Sales Offices at selected places in the country to cater to the needs of the consuming sectors in various regions.</p>

<h2>IMPORT OF COAL</h2>

<p>As per the present Import policy, coal can be freely imported (under Open General Licence) by the consumers themselves considering their needs based on their commercial consideration.</p>

<p>Coking Coal is being imported by Steel sector mainly to bridge the gap between the requirement and indigenous availability and to improve the quality. Other sectors like Power sector, cement etc. and coal traders are importing non-coking coal.</p>

<p>Details of import of coal and products i.e. coke during the last four years including the current year is as under:</p>

<p style="text-align:right"><strong>(Million tonnes)</strong></p>

